{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And he placed it in the basins</b> — these are vessels made unlike the form of the altar vessels, and therefore it says that half the blood, which he intended to throw upon the people, he placed in those vessels, and the other half he threw upon the altar from the sprinkling-basins in which he had received it, in the manner of the offerings. And Ibn Ezra said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 24:6) that the basins were used for both purposes. And so is the opinion of Onkelos (Onkelos on Exodus 24:6), who translated בְּמִזְרְקַיָּא (\"in sprinkling-basins\")."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:15:34.316475523Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}